  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:4684",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with Leucine-rich repeat serine/threonine-protein kinase 2 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets two distinct kinases, LIM domain kinase 2 and Cytochrome P450 2E1, both of which are inhibited by flavopiridol. This indicates that Oblonganoside C may modulate the activity of these kinases, potentially influencing downstream signaling pathways. The shared involvement of flavopiridol as a target of both kinases implies a possible common mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of a consistent score across both paths suggests a plausible biological relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Oblonganoside C in the regulation of Leucine-rich repeat serine/threonine-protein kinase 2.",
